# C046 — runtime-extraction PLAN (NOT built): fold toolfactory's generic credit/keys/billing/logging runtime into Suluk
# packages. Operator-surfaced ("a lot of credit/billing minus topup-subscription pooling+refund, logging, api-key is
# generic, fold it in") + mapped by a code survey (~1,200 LOC generic vs ~400 app-specific) + operator chose "hold,
# record the plan as an ADR first". DISTINCT from C043-C045 (the CI/audit layer): this is the RUNTIME LIBRARY layer.
# DESIGNED-not-built => low ceiling 0.4. NOT a contract facet — app-runtime libs, never touch the matcher (no D1 concern).

# THREE PACKAGES, ADAPTER SEAM, FIXED ORDER. Each = generic logic + an injected DB/Stripe/env handle (the @suluk/deploy/
# stubgen seam); the package owns schema+logic, the app owns the connection+policy. (1) @suluk/credits (~240 + ~110
# logging) — the metered ledger: balance, atomic debitIfCovers (the CAS closing the concurrent-charge window), idempotent
# debit (double-spend guard), per-key spend, txn log, the activity-log query (logging is a read-side projection over the
# ledger); schema credit_transaction/credit_amount/credit_key; stays app: payment-alert kinds; extends @suluk/drizzle;
# the DEPENDENCY ROOT. (2) @suluk/keys (~449, 100% GENERIC, the cleanest) — hierarchical API keys: scopes, delegation
# chain, effective-caps (scope-subset, cap-min, expiry-soonest), POOLED subtree headroom (a parent cap bounds parent+
# children TOTAL spend, abuse-proof), cascade expiry/disable/revoke, lineage, auth middleware; extends @suluk/better-auth
# + @suluk/drizzle; pairs with credits. (3) @suluk/billing (~335) — Stripe plumbing: checkout/PaymentIntent/SetupIntent,
# subscription CRUD, payment methods, refund MECHANICS, tax; stays app (operator exclusions): webhook DISPATCH, pricing
# MATRIX, alerts/email, subscription-pooling + refund WORKFLOW; extends @suluk/stripe + @suluk/drizzle, depends on credits.
# BUILD ORDER credits -> keys -> billing.
claim runtime_extraction_three_packages_decomposition: Bool @>=0.4 = True
falsified_when runtime_extraction_three_packages_decomposition == False

# DESIGNED-NOT-BUILT + LIVE-BILLING CAUTION (honest). The LOC/boundaries are from a SURVEY, re-confirm at build time.
# Building the packages is additive + safe (new, test-witnessed); REWIRING toolfactory's LIVE credit/billing to use them
# is the riskier SEPARATE step — only after each package is byte-faithful to the extracted logic + unit-witnessed; the
# atomic-debit CAS + idempotency are load-bearing for money-correctness. The contract/runtime layers MEET at C044
# settlement (the contract declares the lever; @suluk/credits/@suluk/keys enforce it; rate-limit middleware already ships
# in @suluk/hono, credit debit becomes a thin @suluk/credits call). Deferred to the build session: the exact adapter-seam
# interface per package, Drizzle schema ownership (package-owned vs app-declared), whether @suluk/keys wraps the
# @better-auth/api-key plugin.
claim runtime_extraction_designed_not_built_live_billing_caution: Bool @>=0.4 = True
falsified_when runtime_extraction_designed_not_built_live_billing_caution == False

# C046 BUILD PROGRESS — @suluk/keys PURE CORE built 2026-06-30 (the cleanest, FIRST per the plan). The delegation-chain
# ALGEBRA extracted VERBATIM from the source: effectiveCaps (intersect scopes, min caps/expiry up the chain),
# pooledHeadroom (the ABUSE-PROOF property — a parent cap bounds its WHOLE subtree's total spend, so a key can't multiply
# its budget by minting children), expired/disabledAncestor (the read-time revocation cascade), clampChildGrant, the
# materialized-path utilities (escapeLike/inSubtree/childPath/...), parseScopes/parseKeyMeta (the scope/metadata model,
# reusing @suluk/better-auth permissionsToScopes). PURE — the app builds ChainNode[] + per-path SpendRow[] from its DB
# (the query is the SEAM, deferred per C046) and calls these so the money/abuse-correctness logic can NEVER drift.
# WITNESSED by keys 18 pass (incl. the load-bearing pooled-headroom abuse-proof test: parent cap 50, child spends 30 ->
# parent remaining counts the pooled 50, not its own 20). REMAINING in @suluk/keys: the DB-orchestration seam
# (resolveChain/revokeKeyTree over a KeyStore adapter) + a Drizzle reference impl. NOTE: @suluk/better-auth already
# exports parseApiKeyMetadata — a possible consolidation to check at the credits/orchestration step. credits + billing +
# the toolfactory rewiring remain.
claim runtime_keys_delegation_algebra_core_built: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when runtime_keys_delegation_algebra_core_built == False

# C046 BUILD #2 — @suluk/credits (the DEPENDENCY ROOT) built 2026-06-30. The metered ledger extracted VERBATIM: the
# package OWNS the schema (credit_transaction + credit_amount/credit_key sidecars; userId a plain col — the app owns the
# user table + any FK), the app injects a Drizzle handle (D1 prod, bun:sqlite tests). Money-correctness core: debitIfCovers
# (ATOMIC conditional INSERT — can't drive the ledger negative under concurrency; self-guards a negative amount from
# MINTING), debitOnceIfCovers (INSERT OR IGNORE — the partial-refund double-spend guard: a replay maps to the
# deterministic nonce row, NEVER a second debit), debitOnceAttributed, getBalance/record/recordKey/keySpend, ledgerRow/
# recordAmount, listTransactions (the activity log), ledgerStats (the generic admin aggregate; the user-COUNT stays app),
# addCredits/debitCredits. EXCLUDED (app-specific): payment-alert kinds, the user-table count. deps drizzle-orm +
# @suluk/drizzle. WITNESSED against a REAL bun:sqlite — credits 10 pass (the atomic floor: debit>balance -> false +
# balance unchanged; the idempotent replay -> no second debit; keySpend attribution). REMAINING: the @suluk/keys
# DB-orchestration seam (now buildable — chainHeadroom joins the credit ledger), then @suluk/billing; toolfactory rewiring.
claim runtime_credits_ledger_built_atomic_witnessed: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when runtime_credits_ledger_built_atomic_witnessed == False

# C046 BUILD #3 — @suluk/keys LINEAGE DB OPS + the keys×credits INTEGRATION built 2026-06-30 (completes the generic keys
# surface). @suluk/keys now OWNS the key_lineage schema (the delegation tree) + the materialized-path DB ops over an
# injected Drizzle handle: subtreeOf, parentPathOf, insertLineage (extracted verbatim), revokeKeyTree (cascade with the
# STRICT-descendant guard; the apikey-disable INJECTED so keys stays free of the Better Auth apikey table), and
# chainHeadroom — THE INTEGRATION POINT: it joins @suluk/credits' credit_key + credit_transaction (keys deps credits) for
# per-path spend, then pooledHeadroom -> the abuse-proof cap is REAL end-to-end (a parent cap bounds parent+child TOTAL
# spend). The app-specific grant-fetch (apikey vs MCP tables) stays in the app and CALLS these primitives. deps +=
# @suluk/credits + drizzle-orm. WITNESSED against a REAL bun:sqlite — keys 22 pass (the pooled chainHeadroom = {limit 50,
# spent 40, remaining 10}: 40 = root 30 + child 10, NOT 30; the strict-descendant revoke guard). @suluk/keys generic
# surface COMPLETE (algebra + path + scopes + lineage + headroom). REMAINING: @suluk/billing; the toolfactory rewiring.
claim runtime_keys_lineage_and_credits_integration_built: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when runtime_keys_lineage_and_credits_integration_built == False

# C046 BUILD #4 — @suluk/billing v1 built 2026-06-30 (the LAST extraction package; a BOUNDED, faithful v1). Stripe
# PLUMBING over an injected StripeConfig {secretKey, fetch?}: the HTTP transport (STRIPE_POST/GET verbatim incl the refund
# idempotency-key) + customer/SetupIntent/PaymentIntent creation + the saved-card surface (listPaymentMethods wire-mapping,
# defaultCard/defaultPaymentMethodId, ownsPaymentMethod, setDefaultPaymentMethod, setSubscriptionDefaultCard,
# detachPaymentMethod, setSubscriptionCancel, payOpenInvoice). The res.ok + field-presence + throw semantics PRESERVED
# VERBATIM; the ONLY deliberate change is DROPPING the Effect-Schema defensive response-decode (a robustness layer the app
# re-adds) -> NO `effect` dep. deps @suluk/stripe (toForm). WITNESSED with a MOCK fetch — billing 7 pass (auth header +
# idempotency-key + form body + the wire mapping + the error-throw path). DEFERRED (the careful follow-on, NOT v1, found
# entangled): the money-MOVING paths (createCheckout/chargeOffSession/createPaymentIntentOnDefaultCard — money + metadata),
# the PRICING-WOVEN subscription logic (getSubscriptionStatus/changeSubscriptionPlan use subPlanById/ceilingFor/SUB_PLANS),
# the webhook DISPATCH + creditOnce grant, email, the billing-account DB linking. NOTE: @suluk/stripe already exports
# restStripe/stripeGet — a transport consolidation to check. ALL THREE runtime packages now have shipped cores; the
# toolfactory rewiring (the live-billing cutover) remains the SEPARATE careful follow-on.
claim runtime_billing_v1_transport_and_card_surface_built: Bool @>=0.5 = True
falsified_when runtime_billing_v1_transport_and_card_surface_built == False

# C046 BUILD #5 — @suluk/billing v2: the DEFERRED wrappers FINISHED (2026-07-01), + @suluk/credits gains grantOnce. The
# v1-deferred surface extracted with the SEAM resolving each entanglement, plain-JSON (no effect dep), source res.ok/field
# semantics VERBATIM: (a) payments.ts — the money-MOVING paths (createCheckout / createSubscriptionCheckout /
# createPortalSessionForCustomer / createPaymentIntentOnDefaultCard / chargeOffSession) with the app's product NAME +
# success/cancel/return URLs injected as PARAMS (no app routes/branding baked in); the off-session decline taxonomy
# preserved (authentication_required -> authRequired flag; hard 402 RETURNED not thrown; transient THROWS). (b) tax.ts —
# calculateTax / recordTaxTransaction, graceful (any failure -> taxCents 0, the top-up always proceeds). (c)
# subscriptions.ts — the PRICING-WOVEN logic made GENERIC over a SubPlan CATALOG the app passes (planById/planByPrice over
# the injected SubPlan[], a SubscriptionBranding seam for the Product/lookup_key) + the PURE ceilingFor (paid-ceiling
# math) + ensurePlanPrice/createSubscriptionOnDefaultCard/getSubscriptionStatus/changeSubscriptionPlan — the up>down>up
# never-recharge invariant intact. (d) account.ts — the package-OWNED billing_account store (userId PK plain col; app
# injects a Drizzle handle, exactly like credits/keys) with linkBillingCustomer NEVER clearing a subscriber's sub. The
# "creditOnce" deferred item landed in its RIGHT home: @suluk/credits.grantOnce — the money-IN idempotent grant (legacy-key
# honoured + non-finite/fraction/negative REJECTED), the money-IN twin of debitOnceIfCovers. STAYS APP (policy, not
# library; HONEST): the webhook DISPATCH (composes @suluk/stripe webhookRouter/verifyStripeSignature + these primitives +
# grantOnce + the app's pricing/alerts), the branded email TEMPLATES, the payment-alert kinds, and refund + subscription-
# POOLING (operator-excluded from the start). deps += @suluk/drizzle + drizzle-orm. WITNESSED — billing 29 pass (mock-fetch
# request+response + the off-session taxonomy + the ceilingFor money-math + a REAL bun:sqlite account store), credits 14
# pass (grantOnce idempotency/legacy-key/non-finite), both tsc clean. REMAINING C046: ONLY the toolfactory rewiring (the
# live-billing cutover — the SEPARATE careful step, after each package proves byte-faithful). The library layer is DONE.
claim runtime_billing_v2_deferred_wrappers_finished_and_grantonce: Bool @>=0.55 = True
falsified_when runtime_billing_v2_deferred_wrappers_finished_and_grantonce == False
